{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry","id":1489428,"title":"What is the future of VTM, and the WOD as a whole, within the videogame industry?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-07T14:30:27-07:00","id":1489428,"title":"What is the future of VTM, and the WOD as a whole, within the videogame industry?","content":"Paradox seems to be growing their videogame portfolio, with everything from interactive fiction to a battle royale, it seems like Paradox has done a good job of increasing VTM's, and overall, the WOD's, popularity. However, how long do you think this is going to last for? Almost nobody talks about their interactive fiction games anymore, Swansong doesn't seem to have been well received, Earth blood looks to be a disappointment, and Bloodlines 2 is going through issues of its own. Blood Hunt seems to be the only game that's doing well, which is a mystery to me seeing as how unless you were playing from day one of release, you're going to be dying constantly.<br /> <br /> I actually deleted the game because of how unfriendly the matches were for new players, like seriously, you rarely make a kill, and you will never win a game. Most of the time I would have my Nosferatu just crouch and go invisible, I would eventually get killed, but it would let me outlive many of the other players. Playing like that isn't fun though. I'm pretty sure I'm not the only one who has had this issue either. Rant aside, Paradox seems to be churning out one videogame after another, not all of them seem to be that great, but enough are doing good numbers to seemingly justify making more games.<br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T14:40:38-07:00","id":1489429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry#post1489428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paradox seems to be growing their videogame portfolio, with everything from interactive fiction to a battle royale, it seems like Paradox has done a good job of increasing VTM's, and overall, the WOD's, popularity. However, how long do you think this is going to last for? Almost nobody talks about their interactive fiction games anymore, Swansong doesn't seem to have been well received, Earth blood looks to be a disappointment, and Bloodlines 2 is going through issues of its own. Blood Hunt seems to be the only game that's doing well, which is a mystery to me seeing as how unless you were playing from day one of release, you're going to be dying constantly.<br /> <br /> I actually deleted the game because of how unfriendly the matches were for new players, like seriously, you rarely make a kill, and you will never win a game. Most of the time I would have my Nosferatu just crouch and go invisible, I would eventually get killed, but it would let me outlive many of the other players. Playing like that isn't fun though. I'm pretty sure I'm not the only one who has had this issue either. Rant aside, Paradox seems to be churning out one videogame after another, not all of them seem to be that great, but enough are doing good numbers to seemingly justify making more games.<br /> <br /> What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm inclined to think that a lot will depend on what the reception of <i>Bloodlines 2</i> will be when it's finally released. I'm a lot more positive about the cachet of V:TM as it is but recognize that Earthblood was terrible.<br /> <br /> <i>Swansong</i> and <i>Blood Hunt</i> were never MEANT to be the mainstream representation of V:TM in the media, they were meant to be harmless side games.<br /> <br /> I do think the upcoming television shows, however, will probably be more popular than all of the video games and tabletop games combined, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T15:18:31-07:00","id":1489431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489429#post1489429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm inclined to think that a lot will depend on what the reception of <i>Bloodlines 2</i> will be when it's finally released. I'm a lot more positive about the cachet of V:TM as it is but recognize that Earthblood was terrible.<br /> <br /> <i>Swansong</i> and <i>Blood Hunt</i> were never MEANT to be the mainstream representation of V:TM in the media, they were meant to be harmless side games.<br /> <br /> I do think the upcoming television shows, however, will probably be more popular than all of the video games and tabletop games combined, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The television shows are what scares me the most to be honest, It is very easy to turn the rich universe of WoD into a cheese fest crap of a tv show and to be perfectly honest, most of the new WoD projects aside from L.A. By night and Bloodhunt (still can't believe it), turned out to be crap so I don't really have great expectations...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T15:22:07-07:00","id":1489432,"title":"","content":"The primary problem with Bloodhunt is that it's a Battle Royale game, which are designed to heavily favor skilled FPS players by removing as much as possible that would let another factor dominate a match. It's the Souls franchise approach to multiplayer shooters: die, a lot, until you either give up or get to a competitive level. That's a hurdle to VtM fans looking for a fun videogame for them, but you can't dilute that without turning off the fans of the Battle Royale genre that would be the larger target audience. Bloodlines bigger struggles are that the BR genre is already very crowded, and Bloodhunt is essentially too late to the party to get traction with what it offers to set it apart. <br /> <br /> While perhaps a bit of of sticky comparison, Bloodhunt had the potential to be the equivalent to EVE Online: a small dedicated fanbase to a slightly higher learning curve game than average for the genre, but with enough uniqueness to draw people in and keep them. Much like VtM was never going to unseat D&amp;D as the biggest RPG around, EVE was never really competition for bigger games like WoW. But EVE is a good game that knows it's niche and how to occupy it such that it hasn't gone anywhere (to the point where in some ways it inspires a form of success WoW doesn't: fans that are happy with the game and don't want to find something else after awhile).<br /> <br /> If Bloodhunt came out earlier, I think it would be in a similar position to EVE: a little quirky, a little different, and thus can stand out in the genre as a game that might not be for everyone, but the people it is for love it. But now BR games have already ground through the audience's desire for experimentation of the formula and they just want great versions of what everyone know works (aka the big names stay big because they're that). If a new game wants to break into the genre in a serious fashion, it needs to be great BR game and offer something groundbreaking to be attractive to players. Bloodhunt is a probably on the line between good and great as a BR, but it's features just aren't big enough to make most people stick around. It does do some cool things, but nothing revolutionary.<br /> <br /> --------------<br /> <br /> Honestly I think they should have focused on the asymmetrical action MMO market rather than BR. There's so much more room for innovation in the asymmetrical space, it's a more accessible genre to causal and new players, and it lets you lean into the VtM setting/lore.<br /> <br /> Like, just off the top of my head, instead of the standard &quot;one superpowered bad guy vs. a group of low powered normal folks&quot; model you see in games like Dead by Daylight, you could have a three way match between vampires, hunters, and humans. In a big twist on the genre, the mortal faction of players operate as both cover for the other two (vampires need to hide among humans to avoid getting outnumbered and mowed down, hunters need to hide among humans to successfully find and ambush vampires first), and you can have mortal that ally with the other factions get perks to help them with their own win-conditions (get cool gear from hunters that helps you survive on the grounds that you'll help fight the undead, or become a ghoul for powers of your own).<br /> <br /> You mix together the social intrigue of Among Us, with the horror action of Dead by Daylight, and the neater combat mechanics that went into Bloodhunt instead and you'd have a pretty solid game that would really be unique in a way that could capture a lot of player.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T15:25:14-07:00","id":1489433,"title":"","content":"I mostly (but not completely) agree with the main points of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> here: a lot will depend on <i>Bloodlines 2</i> and, above that, the upcoming TV shows (lets conflate TV and Streaming for ease of reference).<br /> <br /> But first it is important to understand the business model Paradox is using by now. They're not investing in that many video-games. Actually, they didn't invested in anything beyond <i>Bloodlines 2</i>.<br /> <br /> What Paradox does for now is just licensing. You approach them with a project, and they either green-light it or not for using the IP. They get a cut of the profits, but otherwise you're on your own to make the game. Recently they expanded this to make licensing even easier and maybe give some help with your project, but the core idea is the same.<br /> <br /> That's it. Every game we saw is the personal project of an independent developer or small starting company, and the fact they keep coming is just a result of how many people are willing to give it a try. And while the number of projects isn't small, size matters here, no one approached them yet with a big project but <i>Blood Hunt</i> for now, all those games we got are small fries by people with nothing to lose. The lack of robust projects by now is starting to be an issue.<br /> <br /> Paradox <b>is</b> a games company by itself, a rising star at that, just not with anything related to WoD and they didn't put their own studios to work on it aside for <i>Bloodlines 2</i>, which we don't know how much they're actually involved. Their main business for now is occupied with their titles of strategy that are already making good money. I can't blame them, but WoD is actually just a side project.<br /> <br /> For now, the lack of experienced developers with solid projects (not necessarily big) is putting even greater pressure on <i>Bloodlines 2</i>. Unless in their current model they manage to find the rare Indie Gem they're after to change the tides, a lot on the video-game side of their business will depend on <i>Bloodlines 2</i>'s performance.<br /> <br /> On the other side, though, the real big money was always meant to be live action TV. Success in any other field can affect how much they can attract TV projects to begin with, or recover from an eventual blow if their TV debut goes wrong. But a good performance on TV will have a far more palpable effect on everything else. <b>IF</b> they manage to dig gold on TV, then the WoD IP may very well flip to be the most lucrative thing on their hands by now. That's their best bet, and the biggest impact we'll see on the IP's future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T15:28:26-07:00","id":1489434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489429#post1489429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do think the upcoming television shows, however, will probably be more popular than all of the video games and tabletop games combined, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the popularity will depend on which sect and what type of vampire the show follows. The Camarilla and the Anarchs are going to be pretty easy to understand. The Camarilla is all about politics, and the Anarchs are all about revolution and freedom, which a lot of the time seems like Anarchy. The Sabbat on the other hand is a doomsday cult that seem to do evil, for the sake of it. The main character is probably going to be a fledgling, most likely caitiff or thin blood, the audience will learn more about the world of VTM through this unfortunate fledgling.<br /> <br /> The show is probably going to explore the politics that the game is so well known for and have the fledgling in question be pushed into the center of it all. I'm guessing the fledgling will mostly be interacting with the Camarilla if this is true.<br /> <br /> However, I don't really watch tv, instead preferring to spend my time on YouTube, so I may be off with my assumptions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 08-07-2022, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T15:36:14-07:00","id":1489435,"title":"","content":"Bloodlines 2 will have sweet graphics, but the storyline will be terrible because a good ESG score is more important than a compelling game. It will have negative reviews, and all the high powered executives who used to destroy everything they touched by chasing profits and are now destroying everything by chasing above mentioned ESG scores will write the genre off, and V:tM and WOD will survive via crowd sourced text based Choose Your Own Adventure games on your mobile device, available on both Android and iOS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T16:00:26-07:00","id":1489436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489431#post1489431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The television shows are what scares me the most to be honest, It is very easy to turn the rich universe of WoD into a cheese fest crap of a tv show and to be perfectly honest, most of the new WoD projects aside from L.A. By night and Bloodhunt (still can't believe it), turned out to be crap so I don't really have great expectations...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean, I wouldn't WANT it to be Prestige TV.<br /> <br /> It's a game that should be overwhelming full of melodrama, schlock, and backstabbing soap operaness.<br /> <br /> What do YOU think Vampire: The Masquerade the show should be about?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489435#post1489435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bloodlines 2 will have sweet graphics, but the storyline will be terrible because a good ESG score is more important than a compelling game. It will have negative reviews, and all the high powered executives who used to destroy everything they touched by chasing profits and are now destroying everything by chasing above mentioned ESG scores will write the genre off, and <b>V:tM and WOD will survive via crowd sourced text based Choose Your Own Adventure games on your mobile device, available on both Android and iOS.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if you're referring to the Choice of Games Vampire: The Masquerade games or if this is just coincidence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-07-2022, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T16:10:45-07:00","id":1489438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489436#post1489436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I mean, I wouldn't WANT it to be Prestige TV.<br /> <br /> It's a game that should be overwhelming full of melodrama, schlock, and backstabbing soap operaness.<br /> <br /> What do YOU think Vampire: The Masquerade the show should be about?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I wonder if you're referring to the Choice of Games Vampire: The Masquerade games or if this is just coincidence.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe the years of playing Requiem warped my expectations of what a vampire tv show could be but I think that something slightly better than the crap they make on CW could be achieved for vampire, I personally think that a good vampire show should follow a structure similar to the Sopranos with a sprinkle of true detective put in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T16:46:10-07:00","id":1489440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489438#post1489438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the years of playing Requiem warped my expectations of what a vampire tv show could be but I think that something slightly better than the crap they make on CW could be achieved for vampire, I personally think that a good vampire show should follow a structure similar to the Sopranos with a sprinkle of true detective put in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly enough, I basically had a variant on this conversation about what exactly a friend of mine expected a Dungeons and Dragons movie to be.<br /> <br /> <i>Friend: Lord of the Rings shows we can have a serious epic fantasy movie. One with great acting and plots.<br /> <br /> Me: What the hell is wrong with you? God no.<br /> <br /> Friend: What?<br /> <br /> Me: I want a Dungeons and Dragons movie with regular cuts back to the players goofing off, deciding their player characters are in love because they're dating, disappearing from the plot because their players are absent, and Monty Python references.<br /> <br /> Friend: Why the hell would you want that?<br /> <br /> Me: Because I want to capture the spirit of the game and its wackiness.</i><br /> <br /> I mean I don't want it to be What We Do In the Shadows but, well, that's because we already have What We Do in the Shadows and that is the best Sabbat show they could ever do. Why everyone chose to play Old Clan Tzimisce I don't know but it's all the better for it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br