p;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T17:49:45-07:00","id":1489443,"title":"","content":"VTM is getting a TV show??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T17:58:00-07:00","id":1489444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489443#post1489443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">VTM is getting a TV show??</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://winteriscoming.net/2021/04/28/vampire-masquerade-universe-getting-turned-tv-shows-movies-etc/\" target=\"_blank\">https://winteriscoming.net/2021/04/2...ws-movies-etc/</a><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The \u201cWorld of Darkness\u201d began with the Vampire: The Masquerade table-top role-playing game in 1991. Soon there were other titles like Werewolf: The Apocalypse, Mage: The Ascension, Orpheus and Hunter: The Reckoning. There have been World of Darkness video games, novels, and more, with the common thread being that they put monsters and outsiders at the center of the stories.</span></i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>And now, the World of Darkness is getting the cinematic universe treatment courtesy of Oscar-nominated Arrival screenwriter Eric Heisserer, according to <a href=\"https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/heat-vision/world-of-darkness-roleplaying-game-headed-to-film-tv-with-arrival-screenwriter-eric-heisserer\" target=\"_blank\">The Hollywood Reporter</a>. He\u2019ll be working with writer Christine Boylan, who\u2019s worked on whos like The Punisher and Castle. The whole thing will be produced by Hivemind, which is behind shows like The Witcher and The Expanse.</i><br /> <br /> <i>We don\u2019t know exactly what form the World of Darkness cinematic universe will take, but films and TV shows are a good place to start. \u201cThe World of Darkness story universe is deliberately and unapologetically inclusive and diverse,\u201d Boylan said in a statement. \u201cIt has always made a point of including equal gendered characters, protagonists and antagonists of every race, and representation of all creeds \u2014 bringing a female and diverse audience to gaming like nothing prior.<br /> <br /> Its games and fandom are a place where women, POC, and the LGBTQI community feel welcome and we are very proud to bring these stories to life.\u201d</i><br /> <i>Heisserer, who\u2019s also the creator and showrunner behind Netflix\u2019s Shadow and Bone series, was also psyched: \u201cThe legacy of these stories is way ahead of its time, inviting issues and perspectives other games ignored. This feels like the next step for genre.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <i>Finally, Hivemind president and cofounder Jason Brown sold people on Boylan and Heisserer\u2019s Word of Darkness bonafides: \u201cEric and Christine are among the most extraordinary creators working today, and they\u2019re also gamers who have played in WOD since it began. It\u2019s a rare opportunity when the connection between storyteller and story runs this deep, and that is the alchemy which has led to many of our favorite and most culturally resonant franchises.\u201d</i></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T18:46:34-07:00","id":1489445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489444#post1489444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its games and fandom are a place where women, POC, and the LGBTQI community feel welcome and we are very proud to bring these stories to life.\u201d[/I]<br /> <i>Heisserer, who\u2019s also the creator and showrunner behind Netflix\u2019s Shadow and Bone series, was also psyched: \u201cThe legacy of these stories is way ahead of its time, inviting issues and perspectives other games ignored. This feels like the next step for genre.\u201d</i></div> </div> </div> </div>The amount of corpo-speak in this mixed with the fact that the Shadow and Bones adaptation, while visually well done, was not faithful to the source material in favor of the equivalent of racial diversity, makes me worried that this will be another example of telling an alphabet soup story with fangs, rather than a vampire story that happens to have alphabet soup characters. This is in the same vein as the director of Dog Soldiers wanted to make a soldier movie with werewolves, rather than a werewolf movie that had soldiers in it. For some that is a tricky distinction, but it is an important one.<br /> <br /> That is of course before we touch on the elephant in the room, which is that every gaming group makes the game their own. Their own house rules, their own flavor, and most importantly their own decisions on what themes are important. Which means no one vision for a TV show or movie will make most people happy, let alone all the fans. This is the reason why the D&amp;D movies and tv shows have always been sub-par over the decades.<br /> <br /> Why am I getting this uneasy feeling that Kindred: the Embraced will wind up being a high benchmark? Bearing in mind that series had the vampires day walking if they recently fed, no ghouls ever, Gangrel acted like Brujah, Brujah acted like Ventrue, Nosferatu had Protean &amp; Blood Magic, Assamites were shape shifters, neither the Tremere or Malkavians existed, and the previous prince stepped down because it was time to retire due to vampires going into torpor because of age somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T18:58:54-07:00","id":1489446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489445#post1489445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The amount of corpo-speak in this mixed with the fact that the Shadow and Bones adaptation, while visually well done, was not faithful to the source material in favor of the equivalent of racial diversity, makes me worried that this will be another example of telling an alphabet soup story with fangs, rather than a vampire story that happens to have alphabet soup characters. This is in the same vein as the director of Dog Soldiers wanted to make a soldier movie with werewolves, rather than a werewolf movie that had soldiers in it. For some that is a tricky distinction, but it is an important one.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a rather enormous BUT that accompanies worrying about diversity here in the fact that V:TM was notable for being the most diverse game in tabletop gaming history by the time Chicago by Night came out. Gay people, people of color, Asians, bisexuals, and more. It leaned in heavily to the fact vampirism was embraced as both transgressive yet also incredibly accepting in a time when America was coming out of a very conformist reactionary phase in its history.<br /> <br /> Besides, V:TM doesn't have a main plot to adapt so it's almost certainly original characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is the reason why the D&amp;D movies and tv shows have always been sub-par over the decades. </div> </div> </div>While I don't disagree, I also point out the fact the D&amp;D movies were subpar also is why they're subpar. The Dragonlance animated movies could have been awesome but they made some incredibly shitty choices production wise.<br /> <br /> But yes, Penny Arcade agrees with you.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://assets.penny-arcade.com/comics/20210305-r5AgcoWB.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-07-2022, 10:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T00:48:46-07:00","id":1489454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489446#post1489446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a rather enormous BUT that accompanies worrying about diversity here in the fact that V:TM was notable for being the most diverse game in tabletop gaming history by the time Chicago by Night came out. Gay people, people of color, Asians, bisexuals, and more. It leaned in heavily to the fact vampirism was embraced as both transgressive yet also incredibly accepting in a time when America was coming out of a very conformist reactionary phase in its history.<br /> <br /> Besides, V:TM doesn't have a main plot to adapt so it's almost certainly original characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree with handing that entire statement to WW and V:tM.<br /> <br /> It was different for sexuality being more front and center, but not for racial or cultural representation. D&amp;D under TSR had whole settings where africans, asians, and middle eastern groups were the default or only human races/cultures, and this was before V:tM first edition was on its feet. Even Games Workshop with Warhammer Fantasy had diversity on those fronts.<br /> <br /> As for America coming out of a &quot;conformist phase&quot;, that is outright untrue. The 1950s were a conformist phase, the 1960s and 1970s were nothing but social upheaval and recalibration. The 1980s were a business and cold war phase, then the 1990s when V:tM was written and released was a technology revolution. <br /> <br /> As for being transgressive and accepting, once again D&amp;D was letting you play the good, the bad, and the ugly back in the 1980s. You want to be the hero, the rules supported it, if you wanted to be the villain, the rules supported it. The big difference was that D&amp;D didn't bank on emo-goth adult themes outside of Ravenloft, but seeing how D&amp;D had to survive the Satanic Panic, its not like they could be too blatant about those non-heroic options.<br /> <br /> If I was to give credit to what was revolutionary about V:tM I would say it was the Storyteller system, where XP was gained by playing rather than butchering X amount of monsters for Y amount of xp to gain a level and steal all of their stuff. The D10 dot system with difficulty 6 can be learned in a few minutes, where as explaining THAC0 still causes mild forms of PTSD.<br /> <br /> I agree that the shows will probably have original characters, but if the show writers are going to make original characters and don't have a core plot from the WoD to follow, exactly what will differentiate these shows from other vampire shows like Moonlight, True Blood, Angel, Buffy, or Forever Knight?<br /> <br /> The problem is that what makes WoD different is the society of vampires, the factions, the clans, the different powers, the different weaknesses, and how all those things mix together. But you can't front load all of that, which means the writers will shift gears away from the setting and try to swing for the mythical larger audience by trying to check as many boxes on a list somewhere when it comes to viewer demographics all while trying to sprinkle in some setting fluff here and there.<br /> <br /> When we were young, we would say &quot;oh man this is going to be awesome&quot;, now we say &quot;I wonder how badly they are going to screw this up&quot;, and that is coming from someone who isn't a cynic or a pessimist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T04:05:38-07:00","id":1489463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489436#post1489436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div c