olf movie that had soldiers in it. For some that is a tricky distinction, but it is an important one.<br /> <br /> That is of course before we touch on the elephant in the room, which is that every gaming group makes the game their own. Their own house rules, their own flavor, and most importantly their own decisions on what themes are important. Which means no one vision for a TV show or movie will make most people happy, let alone all the fans. This is the reason why the D&amp;D movies and tv shows have always been sub-par over the decades.<br /> <br /> Why am I getting this uneasy feeling that Kindred: the Embraced will wind up being a high benchmark? Bearing in mind that series had the vampires day walking if they recently fed, no ghouls ever, Gangrel acted like Brujah, Brujah acted like Ventrue, Nosferatu had Protean &amp; Blood Magic, Assamites were shape shifters, neither the Tremere or Malkavians existed, and the previous prince stepped down because it was time to retire due to vampires going into torpor because of age somehow.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am actually even more worried now that I read about the screenwriter, It's not even about making it woke (WoD is as woke as they come and has been so since the 90's, they wouldn't be changing the source material much) but the fact that the stuff the guy wrote is not exactly stellar work and that's me being charitable here...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T04:27:32-07:00","id":1489467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_qu