{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T11:54:53-07:00","id":1489573,"title":"","content":"If they do a tv show based on the setting&gt; i do hope that they learned from the missteps of Kindred The Embraced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T13:45:15-07:00","id":1489582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489524#post1489524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In fact, the irony is the nihilism inherent in punk. Punks do not believe the revolution will ever work. So the corporations co-opting it for their own ends is inevitable.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to who exactly? The majority of the OG punk bands were adamantly against the idea that their music was nihilistic. Rather they were calls to action because the systems are broken and need fixing, and punk was a way to express that discontent in a fashion relatable to people.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489573#post1489573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they do a tv show based on the setting&gt; i do hope that they learned from the missteps of Kindred The Embraced.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's kinda hard to fix &quot;main cast member dies suddenly and tragically who played the character that was such a big reason people watched the show they cancelled it rather than trying to continue.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T19:59:38-07:00","id":1489599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489446#post1489446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also point out the fact the D&amp;D movies were subpar also is why they're subpar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's the only true thing said until this point about what to expect.<br /> <br /> D&amp;D and WoD both have the trait of being settings/styles, not stories. It doesn't mean that making a show based on then isn't feasible or that it is easier, it just means that you need to come up with a good story to tell. The D&amp;D movies failed royally because they were badly done, nothing exceptional or inherent to D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> And you can make any kind of story using them, which is also both a feature and a bug. The expectations of the fanbase are a problem only if you commit to fulfilling them, then you'll put yourself in a tough spot. If you make it reasonably clear that your story isn't <b>the</b> story of the setting, but just <b>a</b> story <b>in</b> the setting, then you can attract people based on your genre and proposal and avoid that trap.<br /> <br /> Going right for reference comedy is as much a trap, if not an even bigger one. Yes, it can be done and work, but it is just another genre and will only work in its own context, like any other genre.<br /> <br /> Complaints about corpo-speak and ESG scores are void of merit on themselves. <b>Everything</b> is profit-based. Onyx Path doesn't work for the art more than Warner Bros. do. Artists have families to feed, bills to pay and stakeholders to please if they want to keep making their art. The more your art brings money, the more you can devote your time and energy to it instead of to a main job. The shows, books and comics we love are as much made for profit as the ones we see as sterile and mass-produced. And they may very well <b>have</b> those problems, it is just that what caused those problems wasn't the search for profit, but just sheer stupidity.<br /> <br /> Except, of course, in some cases where we call them like that just because they're meant for a broader audience and stop being interesting <i>for us</i>. Then it is just too tempting to blame corporate interests instead of accepting that there are other people in the world that also deserve to have things they like, and adapting to cater to them is a perfectly valid choice. Fans have a tendency to feel entitled to the IP to the extreme. <b>They're not</b>. <b>We're not</b>.<br /> <br /> Of course the corpo-speak <i>does</i> worries me a little, but just because they're avoiding talking about the show itself, and that's what should be worrying. And ESG scores can be as much a downer or encourage creativity. The whole Silver Age of comics came from the limitations imposed by the Comics Code, and it was far more creative and interesting than the Golden Age (have you ever read a GA comic? I did, and it is mostly lame with a few gems).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489454#post1489454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I was to give credit to what was revolutionary about V:tM I would say it was the Storyteller system, where XP was gained by playing rather than butchering X amount of monsters for Y amount of xp to gain a level and steal all of their stuff. The D10 dot system with difficulty 6 can be learned in a few minutes, where as explaining THAC0 still causes mild forms of PTSD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not even that, not by a mile.<br /> <br /> D&amp;D wasn't the only thing before WoD and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_role-playing_games\" target=\"_blank\">the RPG market already had everything they put in the Storyteller System and a lot more by the dawn of the 90's</a>. Shadowrun did the whole 'add two traits, roll that many dice, state a target number for your difficulty, count on successes' in 1989, if with D6, and other versions of this predated it. We had games that used advanced calculus in the rules for real, and others that ditched dices completely.<br /> <br /> Tracking Backgrounds and increasing traits by playing the story was already in <i>Traveler</i> in 1977. <i>Call of Cthulhu</i> had Sanity and rules for how your actions affect you personally at least since 1981. Simple and highly lethal combat exists since <i>Boot Hill</i>, 1975. Point-based character creation is as old as <i>Superhero: 2044</i> in 1977. Rein-Hagen himself brought the rules and concepts related to having support characters from his previous years with <i>Ars Magica</i>. Even more specific things like rules for characters climbing an in-game rank ladder like Generation and Garou Rank can be traced to sources like <i>Paranoia</i> in 1984. Most of those games had simpler rules than D&amp;D and actually than the Storyteller System. Some have less flaws, too. Many others were more robust and modular, GURPS being from 1985. VtM simply wasn't all that brilliant from a mechanics standpoint.<br /> <br /> If there's one thing I give WoD credit for, is simply for capturing the spirit of the 90's better than any other game at the time. It was the right game at the right time and the right place. Not for any extraordinary merit of its developers (it wasn't bad by any means, though), but simply by happenstance. Yet, it is a merit, an important one, to be in tune with a decade and a specific generation of teenagers. It is a remarkable feat, but one to be understood in its own confines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489549#post1489549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which...makes it sort of not punk, doesn't it?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Also annoyed with Solarpunk)</div> </div> </div> </div>Blame people not getting Cyberpunk for both. And I personally blame this on <i>Cyberpunk 2020</i>.<br /> <br /> Cyberpunk was maybe the last true punk literary genre. But thanks to <i><u>things</u></i> like <i>Cyberpunk 2020</i> people thought that it was just Sci-Fi through a given aesthetics, and that lead to other aesthetically-bound Sci-Fi to be called &quot;-punk&quot; by association regardless of any relationship to actual Punk.<br /> <br /> Also,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489582#post1489582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The majority of the OG punk bands were adamantly against the idea that their music was nihilistic. Rather they were calls to action because the systems are broken and need fixing, and punk was a way to express that discontent in a fashion relatable to people.</div> </div> </div> </div>That.<br /> <br /> Punk literature may seem nihilistic because it plays against a background of the worse the system has to offer, one way or another. On top of that, as it <b>is Punk</b>, it heavily plays with the idea that mainstream moral isn't just flawed, but a part of the system that causes this suffering, so the heroes aren't nice, actual goodness doesn't look good. Yet it is in the end hopeful that the system will eventually fail, catastrophically, setting people free.<br /> <br /> No, there are Posers who'll market the revolution, but the revolution will eventually drown them. Violently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T20:12:41-07:00","id":1489600,"title":"","content":"My general opinion is that they would do better to start adapting things like Dragonlance, Drizzt Do'Urden, and other of their MANY-MANY characters as well as stories than trying to just sell the setting of Dungeons and Dragons.<br /> <br /> Sadly, the CGI and writing choices of the Dragonlance movie killed that.<br /> <br /> Which is a shame as it could have been awesome live action OR animated.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T20:33:18-07:00","id":1489604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489600#post1489600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My general opinion is that they would do better to start adapting things like Dragonlance, Drizzt Do'Urden, and other of their MANY-MANY characters as well as stories than trying to just sell the setting of Dungeons and Dragons.</div> </div> </div> </div>The <i>Dungeons &amp; Dragons</i> cartoon show from the 80's was a huge success back then and stays a huge success today, and it didn't try anything aside selling the setting premises of <i>Dungeons &amp; Dragons</i>.<br /> <br /> It was just a good cartoon. That's all anything need to be. Not any specific setting, story, adventure or character, just a good show/movie <i>on its fucking own</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T20:38:18-07:00","id":1489605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489604#post1489604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <i>Dungeons &amp; Dragons</i> cartoon show from the 80's was a huge success back then and stays a huge success today, and it didn't try anything aside selling the setting premises of <i>Dungeons &amp; Dragons</i>.<br /> <br /> It was just a good cartoon. That's all anything need to be. Not any specific setting, story, adventure or character, just a good show/movie <i>on its fucking own</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean it was a massivee success in Brazil.<br /> <br /> Not so much the rest of the world.<br /> <br /> Part of that was licensing as the makers were furious to discover that Gary Gygax had already sold the toy rights to D&amp;D so they couldn't make any.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T20:39:46-07:00","id":1489606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489600#post1489600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My general opinion is that they would do better to start adapting things like Dragonlance, Drizzt Do'Urden, and other of their MANY-MANY characters as well as stories than trying to just sell the setting of Dungeons and Dragons.<br /> <br /> Sadly, the CGI and writing choices of the Dragonlance movie killed that.<br /> <br /> Which is a shame as it could have been awesome live action OR animated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a more generic &quot;introduction to the Forgotten Realms&quot; movie, like apparently what we're getting with the upcoming D&amp;D movie, is not a bad way to go in an initial &quot;let people get their feet wet,&quot; way. Play up the humor and try and have it mimic the flow of a D&amp;D campaign in order to demonstrate what Dungeons and Dragons is like to people who have no experience with roleplaying in general. But yeah, after that there's a lot of IPs within D&amp;D that they could do things with. Like turning some of the Drizzt novels (Homeland would be perfect) into a series. Or an animated series set in Ravenloft with each episode focusing on different Dark Domains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T16:28:41-07:00","id":1489687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489605#post1489605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean it was a massivee success in Brazil.<br /> <br /> Not so much the rest of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not exactly what I got from my research.<br /> <br /> 8/10 on IMDB, 75% Rotten Tomatoes, several pop up in an English search on Google. Not a stellar success, but enough of a success to almost have received a third season at the time.<br /> <br /> I'm not in any way presuming it had the same success everywhere, but I did my research before posting.<br /> <br /> We are not talking an all or nothing situation, success can exist in plenty degrees. What the D&amp;D cartoon got in the US at the time was more than good enough, and far better than the failures of the two movies. It was solid enough that it could have started something if not for the fact that TSR didn't had any means to capitalize on it at the time (partly due to small size, partly due to the whole IP debacle with Gygax).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T13:50:38-07:00","id":1489926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489606#post1489606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Play up the humor and try and have it mimic the flow of a D&amp;D campaign in order to demonstrate what Dungeons and Dragons is like</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">No. Please no. Listen, I play these games and I find the plethora of actual play podcast insufferable with their slow pacing, endless stream of unfunny jokes, bad accents and constant pop culture references (not everything is &quot;Lovecraftian&quot;) It's not going to go over well with the rest of the world. How about they aim for Lord of the Rings or the first Conan movie. You know, a serious, legitimate movie. Aim as high as you can </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">and try to hit that goal. Also, people don't need to &quot;get their feet wet&quot;. Even my then 56 yr old mother liked LotR and she didn't know what the fuck it was nor most of what was going on. She still felt entertained. She felt sad when Gollum died and thought Aragorn was totally hot.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Btw, &quot;</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Play up the humor and try and have it mimic the flow of a D&amp;D campaign&quot;... isn't that what we got with the D&amp;D movie? I mean Jeremy Irons hamming it up was awesome for the wrong reasons, but the movie sucked.<br /> <br /> Doesn't the dwarf look directly at the camera and says something not funny? Yeah humor and self-awareness, just like a D&amp;D campaign...</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","name":"HeavyWhiskey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T14:06:56-07:00","id":1489932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HeavyWhiskey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489926#post1489926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean Jeremy Irons hamming it up was awesome for the wrong reasons,</div> </div> </div> </div>The only thing in that movie that was reasonably entertaining. Not the worse movie ever, I wouldn't prefer to jump from a bridge than seeing it again, but certainly it sucked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T14:17:56-07:00","id":1489938,"title":"","content":"Or a more recent example: The Witcher show on Netflix is extremely popular and is a serious adaptation of the novels. It's not without levity or some metahumor, but it's a straight up action fantasy series. It's not trying to make it feel like you're playing the video games as you watch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T14:40:23-07:00","id":1489947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489932#post1489932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing in that movie that was reasonably entertaining. Not the worse movie ever, I wouldn't prefer to jump from a bridge than seeing it again, but certainly it sucked.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a low bar don't you think? <br /> <br /> Pick: either you watch the D&amp;D movie or die. Everyone is going to watch the movie.<br /> <br /> However, if I'm given that choice alongside definite proof of an afterlife and me liking said afterlife, I'd jump.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","name":"HeavyWhiskey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T14:47:05-07:00","id":1489949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489938#post1489938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or a more recent example: The Witcher show on Netflix is extremely popular and is a serious adaptation of the novels. It's not without levity or some metahumor, but it's a straight up action fantasy series. It's not trying to make it feel like you're playing the video games as you watch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. I mean it is not that I'm lobbying for super-serious and dreadful movie without humor; Both LotR and Conan have jokes. But they come off as natural banter between characters. Although I can't speak for The Witcher. I only saw the first season when it came out and don't remember much.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","name":"HeavyWhiskey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T14:55:46-07:00","id":1489952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HeavyWhiskey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489926#post1489926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">No. Please no. Listen, I play these games and I find the plethora of actual play podcast insufferable with their slow pacing, endless stream of unfunny jokes, bad accents and constant pop culture references (not everything is &quot;Lovecraftian&quot;) It's not going to go over well with the rest of the world. How about they aim for Lord of the Rings or the first Conan movie. You know, a serious, legitimate movie. Aim as high as you can </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">and try to hit that goal. Also, people don't need to &quot;get their feet wet&quot;. Even my then 56 yr old mother liked LotR and she didn't know what the fuck it was nor most of what was going on. She still felt entertained. She felt sad when Gollum died and thought Aragorn was totally hot.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Btw, &quot;</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Play up the humor and try and have it mimic the flow of a D&amp;D campaign&quot;... isn't that what we got with the D&amp;D movie? I mean Jeremy Irons hamming it up was awesome for the wrong reasons, but the movie sucked.<br /> <br /> Doesn't the dwarf look directly at the camera and says something not funny? Yeah humor and self-awareness, just like a D&amp;D campaign...</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>No, they actually wanted Dungeons and Dragons to be serious.<br /> <br /> Hence the pretentious storyline of controlling dragons.<br /> <br /> They just had a roguish protagonist and comic relief. That's far from a comedy. Mind you, Vox Machina IS a comedy and strangely had a very serious story and is so far the most accepted Dungeons and Dragons adaptation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T14:56:29-07:00","id":1489953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HeavyWhiskey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489947#post1489947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a low bar don't you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a way of saying I wouldn't find it a terrible use of my time, the movie has entertaining enough moments in comparison to complete tedium. Maybe it's better if I say that I'd still prefer to watch it than to watch paint drying on the wall for two straight hours.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I've seen <i>Super Mario Bros.</i>,<i> Street Fighter</i> with Van Dame and more recently <i>Dragon Ball</i>. I'd take the wall anytime if the choice was one of those, and while I wouldn't chose death, I would at least contemplate it...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T14:58:47-07:00","id":1489956,"title":"","content":"You left out Mortal Kombat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T15:07:26-07:00","id":1489957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489956#post1489956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You left out Mortal Kombat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't. It is slightly better as at least it takes itself a tad less seriously and overall delivers exactly what it promises: nonsensical action scenes. It's also reasonably faithful to the original source in comparison. I'd say it is slightly better than <i>Dungeons and Dragons</i>, even.<br /> <br /> But I <b>did</b>, indeed, left out <i>MK: Armageddon</i>. <b>That</b> was a new level of catastrophic cinematic failure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T15:11:20-07:00","id":1489958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489952#post1489952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, they actually wanted Dungeons and Dragons to be serious.<br /> <br /> Hence the pretentious storyline of controlling dragons.<br /> <br /> They just had a roguish protagonist and comic relief. That's far from a comedy. Mind you, Vox Machina IS a comedy and strangely had a very serious story and is so far the most accepted Dungeons and Dragons adaptation.</div> </div> </div> </div>You really need to see that movie again. Mind you, a lot of the &quot;comedy&quot; is unintentional. <br /> <br /> I don't find controlling dragons to be pretentious. As a matter of fact, It makes sense since dragons used to be something to fear and rarely encountered back in 2nde.(maybe some people played differently, but that's what I got from everyone I knew playing the game back then) And if the DM threw one at you, you knew that their boyfriend/girlfriend just broke off with them. <br /> <br /> I don't know what <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Vox Machina is. I'll assume it's a podcast with bad jokes, bad accents and constant pop culture references.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","name":"HeavyWhiskey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T15:20:19-07:00","id":1489959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489938#post1489938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or a more recent example: The Witcher show on Netflix is extremely popular and is a serious adaptation of the novels. It's not without levity or some metahumor, but it's a straight up action fantasy series. It's not trying to make it feel like you're playing the video games as you watch.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is more down to them trying to copy the &quot;Marvel Method&quot;, than any particular vision they had for the D&amp;D movie.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HeavyWhiskey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489958#post1489958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know what <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Vox Machina is. I'll assume it's a podcast with bad jokes, bad accents and constant pop culture references.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>It's the folks of Critical Role making a cartoon series based on their original campaign. It's pretty well made and quite good, even if I really, really don't have patience for their online sessions.Best D&amp;D adaptation we've had so far.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T15:40:44-07:00","id":1489960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489959#post1489959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the folks of Critical Role making a cartoon series based on their original campaign. It's pretty well made and quite good, even if I really, really don't have patience for their online sessions.Best D&amp;D adaptation we've had so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Critical Role is the name of the podcast and Vox Machina is the name of the campaign? It has bad jokes and constant pop culture references, doesn't it?<br /> <br /> Just so everyone understands me, I was already in my late teens when Buffy started airing, so I I didn't like it and I don't need everything to be goofy, self-aware with constant quips. (I'm not saying that older people can't enjoy that. I'm just saying I didn't grew up with or influenced by it)<br /> <br /> And yes, I blame Buffy and Joss Whedon.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","name":"HeavyWhiskey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T15:59:12-07:00","id":1489967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HeavyWhiskey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489960#post1489960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Critical Role is the name of the podcast and Vox Machina is the name of the campaign? It has bad jokes and constant pop culture references, doesn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well you'll have to survive the first episode as far as juvenile jokes go, but it gets pretty decent and is mostly self referrential or D&amp;D trope referrential rather than pop culture references<br /> <br /> As for what Critical Role is... it's an extremley well produced series of online games starring popular voice actors and has became a cultural juggernaut which is currently the biggest gateway into the roleplaying hobby. Their viewing numbers are off the charts and are something everyone else aspires to. So ignore them at your own choice, just be aware that this is the new gateway to RPG's for the people of today. (we're talking about a million people viewing episodes of this stuff)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T16:04:48-07:00","id":1489968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489967#post1489967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well you'll have to survive the first episode as far as juvenile jokes go, but it gets pretty decent and is mostly self referrential or D&amp;D trope referrential rather than pop culture references<br /> <br /> As for what Critical Role is... it's an extremley well produced series of online games starring popular voice actors and has became a cultural juggernaut which is currently the biggest gateway into the roleplaying hobby. Their viewing numbers are off the charts and are something everyone else aspires to. So ignore them at your own choice, just be aware that this is the new gateway to RPG's for the people of today. (we're talking about a million people viewing episodes of this stuff)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be inclined to believe I wouldn't like it, but if it is very popular and helps people get into the hobby I'm okay with that. Even if it teaches bad table habits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","name":"HeavyWhiskey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T16:08:13-07:00","id":1489969,"title":"","content":"The only bad table habit is if people aren't having fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T16:17:51-07:00","id":1489970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489969#post1489969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only bad table habit is if people aren't having fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to break out in hives when people tell me all about their abomination antedelluvians who reached Golconda and can now do True Magic and are beloved by Changelings everywhere. But as long as everyone is happy with that at their table, go nuts. Your game, your fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T16:48:24-07:00","id":1489978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489969#post1489969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only bad table habit is if people aren't having fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which includes me setting up a horror atmosphere, saying so, creating tension by having the characters get chased by something horrific and being unable to escape trying to open a locked door and someone going: &quot;hmm Do or do not, there is no try, hmmm HMMMM&quot; Now <b>I'M</b> not having fun and neither is the rest of the group.<br /> <br /> That's what I mean by bad table habits. Not <i>how</i> others play at their table. I don't care about that. Have all the fun you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","name":"HeavyWhiskey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T22:08:34-07:00","id":1489998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489970#post1489970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to break out in hives when people tell me all about their abomination antedelluvians who reached Golconda and can now do True Magic and are beloved by Changelings everywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that more or less the description of your average Exalted starter characters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T23:32:06-07:00","id":1490000,"title":"","content":"I admit, I wanted to play a Gangrel who was trained by Predator as one of their own. The ST hated it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T01:32:46-07:00","id":1490005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-videogame-industry?p=1489998#post1489998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't that more or less the description of your average Exalted starter characters?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. The equivalent of that would be the Sidereal born that Exalted as a Solar, who sold himself to Mafeas, and then redeemed himself fixing both the Curse and his Akumadom.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489428-what-is-the-future-of-vtm-and-the-wod-as-a-whole-within-the-